---
title: Overview
description: What the bookkeeping workbench is and how its steps are arranged.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

The bookkeeping workbench is where the books of one company are kept for one period. Each period is handled in a bookkeeping case. The workbench takes the period from the source documents to the reports and, for a GST-registered company, to the GST F5 return.

{% screenshot id="bookkeeping/overview-steps" caption="The step bar at the top of the workbench." /%}

## The steps

The steps are shown from left to right at the top of the workbench:

| Step | What it is for |
|---|---|
| **1 Documents** | Upload, read and classify every document of the period: bank statements, sales invoices, purchase invoices, payroll and other records. |
| **2 Reconcile** | Match bank lines to invoices and bills, post what has no document, and complete the bank reconciliation for each account and month. |
| **3 Review** | Book the period-end adjustments, review the manual changes, check the F5 and complete the period. |
| **4 Report** | Read and export the management accounts, the F5 report, the trial balance, the control accounts and the ledger detail. |
| **5 Year end** | Shown only in the last quarter of a financial year: the year close and the year-end deliverables (financial statements, AGM documents and tax). |

**Company setup**, at the right end of the step bar, holds the settings that belong to the company rather than to one period: onboarding, the company profile, the bank account register, the chart of accounts and the rules.

**Client queries**, at the top right, can be opened from every page of steps 1 to 3.

## Reading the counts on the steps

A red number on a step is the number of items in that step that still need action. The count includes items on hold: an item that is set aside is not finished. A step without a number has nothing left to do.

On **Review**, the small text under the step name shows how many quarter checks are not yet met (for example "3 quarter checks not met").

## Interface language

The **English | 中文** switch at the end of the step bar changes the interface language at once, without reloading the page. Open drawers and dialogs stay open. The interface language does not change the language in which the AI employee replies in chat; see the [FAQ](/en/bookkeeping/faq/).

## Quarterly bookkeeping and annual bookkeeping

A company is kept either quarter by quarter or once a year, according to its settings.

- **Quarterly bookkeeping** uses the step names in this manual: Documents, Reconcile, Review and Report. Each quarter is completed and locked on its own. The last quarter of a financial year also has the Year end step.
- **Annual bookkeeping** covers a whole financial year in one case. Step 2 is named **Listings** and has four tabs (Bank, Sales, Purchases and Journal), and step 3 is named **Review**. The operations are the same as described in this manual.

{% aside type="tip" %}
Start each working session with the client query list: record any replies from the client first, then work on the to-do items. See [Ask the client](/en/bookkeeping/client-queries/).
{% /aside %}
